The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the code in this repository. It does not cover
the data.

The Bank Account Fraud (BAF) dataset is published separately by its authors and
carries its own terms, stated on its Kaggle page:

    https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/sgpjesus/bank-account-fraud-dataset-neurips-2022

No BAF data is included in this repository -- not the raw CSVs, not the interim
parquet, not a sample. CI fails the build if any appears. What is committed is
aggregate output computed from it: metric summaries, the alpha sweep, the
figures. Anyone wanting the data should download it from Kaggle under those
terms; `make data` does exactly that and verifies the checksums.

Citation for the dataset:

    Jesus et al., "Turning the Tables: Biased, Imbalanced, Dynamic Tabular
    Datasets for ML Evaluation", NeurIPS 2022.
    https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.13358
